==English==
{{wikipedia}}
===Etymology===
From {{term|extreme}} + {{suffix|-o-|phile}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{biology}} An [[organism]] that [[live]]s under [[extreme]] [[condition]]s of [[temperature]], [[salinity]] etc; commercially important as a [[source]] of [[enzyme]]s that operate under similar conditions.
#*'''2003''', {{w|Bill Bryson}}, ''A Short History of Nearly Everything'', BCA, p. 207:
#*:They had found the world's first '''extremophiles''' – organisms that could live in water that had previously been assumed to be much too hot or acid  or choked with sulphur to bear life.

